~ start 

do GameDialogueManager.is_override=true
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("Mysterious Person")
Mysterious Person : Goodness! You're finally awake. Time to stop these vermin from reaching the server!
Mysterious Person : I thought I had lost you!
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=false
Player: Wait, who are you?
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=true
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("Mysterious Person")
Mysterious Person: Right..
Mysterious Person: I forgot to introduce myself.  My name is Odysseus. I will be your Guide!
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=false
Odysseus: I have been protecting the SERVER for so long. Thankfully, you are here now! 
Player: What? Wait, where are we?
do GameDialogueManager.move_camera(240,135,1.5)
Odysseus: Save the chatter for later! See those? Ohh, Spams! They come unwelcome, unsolicited, and in large quantities. So be ready!
do GameDialogueManager.show_enemy("spam", 0)
do GameDialogueManager.start_wave()
=> END

#~ server_health
#Odysseus: Can you see the server's health? It helps you visualize how many beatings it takes before the SERVER collapses. You don’t want to let it drop to 0! 
#Player: These things are so annoying.
#Guide: Spam incoming, get ready.
#=> END

~ spam_filter
Odysseus: Good choice! That tower is called Spam Filter; this was specifically built for this cyber threat.  They have automated security tools that identify, block, redirect, or allow bulk, unwanted, or malicious emails.
Player: Since when do cyberthreats turn into monsters? 
Odysseus: I'll explain later. 
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=true
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("Upgrade")
Odysseus: Now, each enemy drops money and exp points for you to upgrade your towers. Let's ramp up its damage before we get overtaken by them.
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=true
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("TowerUpgrade")
Odysseus: Each tower upgrade is important to make your offense stronger. By maxing the upgrades from the first tier, you can unlock upgrades of a stronger caliber.
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("ServerHp")
Odysseus: Also, can you see the server's health? It helps you visualize how many beatings it takes before the SERVER collapses. You don’t want to let it drop to 0! 
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=false
Player: These things are so annoying.
Guide: Spam incoming, get ready.
do GameDialogueManager.pause_game(false)
=> END

~ spam_defeat
Odysseus: That was close!
Player: Upgrading the canon saves us from that cliff. It really does keep these threats at bay!
Odysseus: Now, don't be hasty; there are many cyber threats out there that you have not encountered yet. Each of them has ways to find weaknesses in your defense and evolve to find an exploit in your system. This does not mean that these threats will stay the same as you encounter them.
Player: It's about time that you do the explaining on what on earth is happening!
#insert function that starts cutscene
do GameDialogueManager.pause_game(true)
do GameDialogueManager.play_scene("1st_scene")
=> END

~ backstory
Player: Why am I not able to remember anything? The last thing I remember was waking up from a headache.
Odysseus: That is not unusual. A lot of people suffer from different side effects of the artificial magnetic field generated by 10 interconnected S.E.R.V.E.R across the globe.  
Player: Did you say 10?
Odysseus: Yes, to mimic the natural magnetic field of Earth. Normally, a single server is enough. But having a single cell battery powering a huge mechanism will only last a century, and there is no safety net in case of malfunction. It is also important to keep threats from monopolizing territories and getting even stronger.
Spam: SNARL…
Player: Speaking of the devil
Odysseus: Brace for another wave!
#insert function that starts cutscene
do GameDialogueManager.start_wave()
=> END

~ wave2_defeat
Player: With the core gone, they turn to the closest replica of power they sought…
Odysseus: Yes, the S.E.R.V.E.R

Player: Wait, wait, wait! That would eventually lead to Earth's collapse. How would it benefit them if they did not have the environment to live in?
Odysseus: They believe that with enough power, they would be able to conquer worlds and travel light-years to search for more power. 
Player: What if they ate the sun?


~ player_level
do GameDialogueManager.delay_dialogue(1.0)
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=true
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("Level")
Odysseus: This gauge gets filled up when you defeat enemies. When it gets full, 
do GameDialogueManager.show_character("Core")
Odysseus: it will give you a core to upgrade your server.
do GameDialogueManager.is_override=false
Player: Bring it on!
do GameDialogueManager.start_wave()
=> END

~ server_upgrade
do GameDialogueManager.delay_dialogue(2.0)
do GameDialogueManager.pause_game(true)
Odysseus: You’ve leveled up! You can now upgrade the server!
do GameDialogueManager.pause_game(false)
do GameDialogueManager.delay_dialogue(1.0)
do GameDialogueManager.move_camera(2851.0,1564.0, 2.0)
do Data.toggle_server_scene.emit()
Odysseus: The server upgrades are a game-changer. It can amplify the damage of your towers, improve your overall defenses, and manage your resource economy. Be wise about where to spend those upgrades!
=> END

~ wave3_defeat
do GameDialogueManager.move_camera(240,135,1.5)
Player: Why cyberthreats?
Odysseus: What?
Player: I mean, why not a mechanical robot like Dungam?
Odysseus: Preference perhaps? I mean, since they want to infiltrate a S.E.R.V.E.R, they want to resemble what a technology fears the most. 
do GameDialogueManager.toggle_fade_transition()
do GameDialogueManager.delay_dialogue(3)
	
~ preparation
Player: Fighting non-stop really takes a toll on your energy.
Odysseus: It really does. But it seems things have settled down for a bit. 
Player: It might be the calm before the storm. Better get ready before threats swarm their way in!
Odysseus: Now that’s the mindset of a strategist! Contingent planning and anticipating cyber attacks are important to minimize damage and to have room to formulate smart decisions on how to deal with the unforeseen. 
if ((Data.maxserverload - Data.currentserverload) < 15 or Data.money < 30) and !GameDialogueManager.is_prep and !Data.is_sandbox and Data.current_wave == 4
	do GameDialogueManager.toggle_fade_transition()
	do GameDialogueManager.delay_dialogue(3)
	do GameDialogueManager.show_dialogue_preparation_end()
	
=> END

~ preparation_end
Odysseus: The threats are already inside the perimeter. Press START to commence.
VIRUS: 010101… INfeCt tHe sYSTem....
do GameDialogueManager.show_play()
#function to activate virus pop-up card
do GameDialogueManager.is_autoplay = false
do GameDialogueManager.show_enemy("virus", 1)
=> END

~ virus
Player: Well, this is new.
Odysseus: Those are Virus. They are malicious software that can infect our defenses, steal information, weaken our towers and damage and disrupt  the server.
=> END

~ firewall
Player: What is this?
Odysseus: You've unlocked a new skill, the Firewall. Let's START the wave for you to know how it actually works.
do GameDialogueManager.start_wave()
do GameDialogueManager.delay_dialogue(1)
Player: Woah! They became faster!
Odysseus: Quick! Deploy the Firewall!
=> END

~ firewall_activated
Odysseus: Firewall prevents unauthorized traffic from entering the system while maintaining a connection with authorized traffic. It slows down the enemies, giving our defenses more time to eliminate them before reaching the SERVER.
=> END

~ server_upgrade2
Odysseus: There is a S.E.R.V.E.R. update now.
do Data.toggle_server_scene.emit()
=> END

~ server_open_cyber
do GameDialogueManager.delay_dialogue(1)
#insert function that opens the server, on the threat page
Player: Player: Now this is new.
Odysseus: Even I didn't know about that. I guess the S.E.R.V.E.R can scan the threats of their current strength after being defeated. It does not show other threats yet.
Player: This might come in handy! Once the threats have been detected and countered, data about them is now available.
=> END

~ adware
do GameDialogueManager.pause_game(true)
Player: What’s that?
do GameDialogueManager.show_enemy("adware",2)
#insert function to activate adware pop-up card
=> END

~ adware2
Odysseus: That is an Adware. They may not look dangerous, but don’t get yourself too comfortable. They slow down operation by showing an ad and redirection. Their slowing capability can make it easier for the enemy to reach our server. 	
=> END

~ specialist
Odysseus: I was wondering when it will be open. It looks like you have unlocked the Analysts' Room.
Player: Analysts Room??
Odysseus: Yes, it is a hidden Specialized Facility connected to the SERVER network. It contains only the best of the best Specialists to help our defenses.
#function to enter analyst room
Player: What are these silhouettes?
Odysseus: AHA! Those are the Threat Hunters, Malware Analysts and many more Specialists waiting to be deployed.
=> END

~ specialist_2
Odysseus: That’s a purple one. You are very lucky!
#function to show ethical hacker
Player: The Ethical Hacker!
Odysseus: Ohhh that’s a good one! Ethical Hackers are cybersecurity experts who legally intrude on a computer or network to find weaknesses to provide a comprehensive way to further improve a system. 
Odysseus: The ethical hacker opens the sandbox mode where you can simulate a battle with all the resources. Isn’t that a perk? What an overview you can get to achieve a better win!
Odysseus: Specialists fight directly on the Battlefield. They can be dragged and dropped anywhere on the map, command their abilities, and can be resurrected again if defeated in a certain amount of time.
=> END

~ Boss1
do GameDialogueManager.pause_game(true)
do GameDialogueManager.camera_shake()
Unknown: *⚠️honk⚠️*
do GameDialogueManager.camera_shake()
Unknown: *⚠️honk⚠️*
do GameDialogueManager.camera_shake()
Unknown: *⚠️honk⚠️*
Player: What’s happening?
System: Warning. High-Threat enemy detected.
Odysseus: This Warning, I have not seen this in decades.
Player: What is it?
Odysseus: It’s one of the earliest cyberthreats to occur, yet crippled millions of computers, costing billions of global damages.
#insert function to show effects
System: Threat Identified: ILOVEYOU Virus
Player: Well, that does not sound threatening at all.
Odysseus: That is exactly why it is dangerous.
do GameDialogueManager.show_enemy("ilu", 14)
=> END

~ Boss1_2
Player: So it is deceptive.
Odysseus: Precisely. 
=> END

~ Boss1_defeated
Player: Pheww. It’s finally over.
Odysseus: Only for now.
System: Boss Remnant recovered.
Odysseus: Looks like you got the remnant of the Virus.
System: Scriptures of the Past unlocked.
System: Scripture I obtained.
#insert function to show scripture
do GameDialogueManager.pause_game(true)
